The eight selected official source/license files bind Excalidraw0.18.1 commit `a2ec2889babf7d2295469c6d90ebe77fae57df84`, MIT. Full files and copyright/license headers survive unchanged. `NOTICE.md` identifies exact source slices and adapters. Runtime is source-assisted new code; no clean-room claim. The existing app `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICE.md` remains unchanged and the public retained LICENSE is independently mapped. Root may link the finite supplement/notice from current metadata without altering historical bytes.

The first source-assisted candidate had three recorded author comparison negatives; the independent review retained a real fractional signed-line last-bit discrepancy and three corrected reviewer UI-premise failures. The corrected stage's old-layout baseline had28/30 pass,23/24 review packets exact and1,755/2,000 new fractional pairs exact. Its corrected30/30 result and independent6fresh+12replay+1diagnostic19/19 acceptance remain separate epochs. No tolerance or numeric serialization normalization was used. Do not discard failures, call replay fresh, or sum overlapping comparisons into universal coverage.

Six alignments and two distributions arrange editable outer groups with signed line/freehand bounds, one-step history and native geometry projection. Mixed opaque groups or selected external bindings refuse. Coordinate/shape/group/point limits remain the existing finite app limits. Arithmetic remains binary64 with source operation order; direct extrema do not establish universal numerical stability. Core hit/render/SVG bounds stay unchanged. No full renderer/binding/frame/rotation, native rough/text/pressure rendering, original GUI, accessibility/usability, memory/performance/reliability superiority or full product parity is established. Pending real browser acceptance must be attached as a distinct future epoch.

The payload triage finds no MZ/PK/GZIP/7z/ELF prefixes, archive/executable paths or selected private-key/token patterns. It retains deliberate author workspace paths/process timestamps and synthetic fixture data as forensic provenance; this is not an exhaustive secret/personal-data certification. No native packages are generated. Exact original159 sourceID/SHA and232 capability IDs are unchanged in `requirements-binding.json`; `proposed-requirements-supplement.json` is prospective work-only information and adds nothing to those live counts.

